# Phase 9 (docs/phase9-brief.md 7.3, 7.8, 8 "Boot allocations and opens"):
# boot to the main menu, then dump every live buflib allocation and the
# file opens since boot. One of the five --ram=32 smoke scripts
# (ipodui-p9-smoke-*), and the before/after artifact for criterion 3:
# with the trims on, no browser cache (tree_mem_init, 300,000 B), skin or
# backdrop buffer, iAP or dircache allocation may appear.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p9-smoke-boot.script
# needs: library
# log: p9 alloc total=
# log: p9 opens=
# log: ipodui: boot variant
# nolog: splash-pass
# golden: skip main
#
# The boot line "ipodui: boot variant <IPOD_VARIANT>" is ui_log()'s
# (ipodui.log on the device); any variant, since the --ram=32 smoke run
# shares this script.
# alloc_dump/open_count: uisimulator/common/sim_cmd_p9.c. name= is the
# allocation's buflib_callbacks symbol (buflib keeps no names).

wait 5000           # boot to the main menu (5 s: 16 parallel sims)
wait_db 30000       # database built (shots.sh primes it if missing)
alloc_dump
open_count
shot main
quit
